 "claims": [
  {
   "label": "Observed",
   "text": "Of the 6 changed files, the production files are ['packages/three-surface-poc-core/src/markdown-code-context.ts', 'packages/three-surface-poc-core/src/project-shape-extraction.ts']; no other non-test file changes in the code commit. The evidence directory is added after it."
  },
  {
   "label": "Observed",
   "text": "The argument-spread census (spread_sweep.py, its regex verbatim) over 257 tracked files finds 33 calls at the base and 31 at the code commit; removed: [['packages/three-surface-poc-core/src/markdown-code-context.ts', 'out.push(...pending.map(blank));'], ['packages/three-surface-poc-core/src/project-shape-extraction.ts', 'all.push(...result.items);']]; added: []. The other 31 are syzygy-bpyt.54 and are untouched."
  },
  {
   "label": "Observed",
   "text": "At the base, scanActiveContent and buildProjectShape throw RangeError (Maximum call stack size exceeded) for a closed fence of 200,000 lines in LF, CRLF and CR, in a phase-B source (vision.md) and in the phase-A root index; at the code commit every one of those 12 builds returns an observed shape with the source classified, with the same 14 cat-file calls as the 100,000-line builds."
  },
  {
   "label": "Observed",
   "text": "At the base, buildProjectShape throws for a success list of 130,000 and of 200,000 bullets (520,272 and 800,272 UTF-8 bytes, under maxBytesPerSource) and returns for 125,000; at the code commit all of 100,000, 125,000, 130,000 and 200,000 return an observed shape with every item."
  },
  {
   "label": "Observed",
   "text": "The boundary is a measurement of a run, not a constant: the first throwing inner-line count was 125,285 (CR) to 125,287 (LF and CRLF) in a vitest process, 125,457 to 125,465 in a bare node process, and it scales with the V8 stack size (about 62,490 at --stack-size=492, 125,460 at the default 984, 251,409 at 1968)."
  },
  {
   "label": "Observed",
   "text": "The mask differential of syzygy-bpyt.16, unchanged, run between the base build and the code commit build over its 11,054 synthetic texts, returns 0 refuses, 0 accepts, 0 same-decision-other-findings and 11,054 unchanged, with C1 to C4 at 0 failures. Every output the change alters is therefore a throw that becomes a decision, at a fence or class past the stack boundary."
  },
  {
   "label": "Observed",
   "text": "Rule 6: six mutants (two restore a spread, four are off-by-one or order faults of a loop) are all killed, and restoring both spreads fails 20 of the new tests; the control run at the code commit fails none."
  },
  {
   "label": "Observed",
   "text": "Two canary tests (one spread call over 200,002 and over 130,002 arguments still throws RangeError in the test process) pass under the configured forks pool and are the only failures under vitest --pool=threads, where a 4 MB worker stack lets the old line pass the size tests (canary-threads-pool.txt)."
  },
  {
   "label": "Observed",
   "text": "A 130,000-item success list makes a shape whose JSON is 227,519,062 bytes, against maxMachineResponseBytes 16,777,216 and maxHumanResponseBytes 2,097,152."
  },
  {
   "label": "Inferred",
   "text": "Because routes.ts serializes the model for the machine routes and bounds each response (a breach answers HTTP 503 with served nothing), a daemon that now starts on such a repository would answer those routes with that 503. Not run: no route or daemon was exercised on a model of that size."
  },
  {
   "label": "Inferred",
   "text": "Startup: createReobserveSession builds the first model inside serveBoundRepository, so a build that no longer throws lets the daemon start where it exited 1 with an observation failure; re-observation of the same input returns reobserved where it returned failed and kept the prior model (the second is run through createReobserveState; the first is read from the code)."
  },
  {
   "label": "Unknown",
   "text": "The effect on any real repository: no repository body was read, every text is synthetic. Whether any observed repository holds a fence or a class that large is not measured."
  }
 ],
